  "focused_log": "crates/compute-mlx/qualification/low-attention-focused.txt",
  "focused_log_sha256": "f05d036a7993d34c2af721269d6c6b113dcd6933744b2ca5c6cd3d2246df453e",
  "notes": [
    "Four new low-attention tests and shared conformance passed on the first actual Metal run; no numerical tolerance changes.",
    "All Q/K/V loads are native low-format. One streaming custom kernel writes f32 output directly without full conversion or score/probability tensors.",
    "BF16 subnormal times large Q/K products, both operand orders, extreme V, dropped early tiles and f32 mask precision passed the independent shared fixture.",
    "Full 64-test regression includes the shared integer power-of-two codec extraction. A test-only unit-variant pattern was then simplified for strict Clippy, and the final four focused tests passed again.",
    "No MLX low-attention performance measurement was made."
  ],
